A PAC–Bayes analysis asks how much information a data-informed randomized predictor uses relative to a prior. Begin with the [Kullback–Leibler divergence](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kullback%E2%80%93Leibler_divergence), then watch it enter a finite change-of-measure calculation.

